  "limitations": [
    "The20 mismatch seeds are dependent nuisance variations. Correct and no-animal predictions are identical across their20 repeated slots and count once for effect heterogeneity.",
    "A top-k share of net benefit can exceed100% because harmed compounds subtract from the total. Positive-only and net-denominator shares are both given to avoid misleading concentration claims.",
    "Top-ranked compounds are descriptive examples, not a premeasurement recommendation or a new confirmed subgroup.",
    "The chemical/context query features remain fixed during animal mismatch. The substituted rat profile belongs to a different compound, so molecular/source compatibility is intentionally broken; this is a predictive negative control, not an exact causal or conditional-randomization intervention.",
    "Rowwise same-time/same-rat-molar exchanges do not preserve a single donor-compound trajectory across a query compound time/dose sequence.",
    "The paired-exposure sensitivity changes both training and evaluation support. Its lower absolute MSE and smaller cohort cannot be treated as a controlled effect of tighter matching alone.",
    "Historical joint RMA, prior outcome inspection, condition-level replicate averaging, one animal species and one broad liver context remain limitations.",
    "Correct pairing outperforms all tested mismatched seed runs in both regimes. In the stricter regime, wrong-fit/correct-query still modestly outperforms the specified prior; pairing loss must not be described as universally removing all animal-associated gain."
  ]
